<title>UK: British unemployment falls by 40,800 in October.</title>
<headline>British unemployment falls by 40,800 in October.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>British unemployment in October fell to 7.2 percent, the lowest level since February 1991, compared to 7.4 percent the previous month, the Office for National Statistics said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The number of unemployed in October fell by 40,800 to 2.03 million.</p>
</text>
